The validation preventing lot variation from matching the canonical lot number is found in **LotVariationsClient.tsx:112-115**:

```typescript
// Check if variation matches canonical lot
if (formData.variationNumber.trim() === selectedLot.lotNumber) {
  return `Cannot be the same as canonical lot (${selectedLot.lotNumber})`
}
```

This validation is implemented in the `validationError` useMemo (LotVariationsClient.tsx:102-124) and also enforced again in the `handleCreate` function (LotVariationsClient.tsx:244-252). The check compares the trimmed variation number against the selected canonical lot's `lotNumber` property, preventing users from creating a variation that matches the canonical lot. The validation error is displayed in real-time in the form UI (LotVariationsClient.tsx:581-589) and blocks form submission by disabling the create button (LotVariationsClient.tsx:654).
